# CHIME CIRCUIT: the CPUs' temper is drawn once for the whole race, not
# every few seconds: half the races are calm (they let you by), a third
# are mixed (some jostle), the rest are mean, with one hunter at most; on
# TWIN FLUE every race is mean, with two hunters. A jostler swings at a
# player in reach now and then (one frame in twenty), but never at a ship
# that is lapping it; only a hunter does that. A hunter that lands a knock
# lets its prey go for four seconds.
game chime
wait 30
# a calm race stays calm
seed 1
cheat race 2
expect temper == 0
expect hunters == 0
botplay 1500
expect aggro1 == 0
expect aggro2 == 0
expect aggro3 == 0
expect aggro4 == 0
expect aggro5 == 0
# a mixed one: some jostle, nobody hunts, and it stays that way
seed 2
cheat race 2
expect temper == 1
expect hunters == 0
expect aggro1 == 1
expect aggro5 == 1
botplay 1500
expect aggro1 == 1
expect aggro5 == 1
expect hunters == 0
# a mean one: a single hunter, the rest jostle
seed 7
cheat race 2
expect temper == 2
expect hunters == 1
expect aggro5 == 2
botplay 1500
expect hunters == 1
expect aggro5 == 2
# TWIN FLUE: always mean, two hunters
seed 1
cheat race 6
expect temper == 2
expect hunters == 2
seed 2
cheat race 6
expect temper == 2
expect hunters == 2
# a jostler alongside a player (after the opening scrum) swings at it
seed 1
cheat race 1
cheat park_cpus
cheat go
wait 320
cheat place 1 120 30
cheat aggro 1 1
cheat revive 0
cheat revive 1
